v1.0
====

I've released this version which has been thoroughly tested.

It's  not flash, I do have ideas on where I want it to go.  I'd like to see
it  more  configurable,  and I have made it easy to do just that.  I'd also
like to perhaps look at sorting the files.

The idea behind VegFL came from me using CList with CNet/3.  It was a great
file  lister.   With  CNet/4  I  wanted  a file lister that was written for
CNet/4.   Also, I have a lot of files and subboards and some of them are on
partitions  which  are  actually NFS partitions.  So I needed a CNetC style
program,  but  one  that took into account that not all of us have heaps of
memory.   I  have on average 4MB free and VegFL barely touches any of this.
Speed  is sacrificed, but then this is a file lister that is designed to be
run  by as a cron event.  It will run through 850 subboards, work out which
subboards are to have the files listed and then list about 11,000 files all
in  about  3 and a half minutes on my A4000/040 (C= 040).  So it's not that
slow.

VegFL is compiled on an A4000/040 using SAS/C v6.51

Installation: VegFL is a DOS file. It can be run from within CNet (AO it
              as a DOS file) or run it from a cron (CNet's cron is v.good).
              The files VegFL and VegFL.cfg must be in the same directory.
              Put them wherever you want. I put them in Doors:VegFL/
              **IMPORTANT** Make sure VegFL.cfg's first line reflects the
              path and file name of the header file for the list. For example:
              
              bin:header.txt 
              
              The next line is the access level to have the files of a 
              subboard listed. By this I mean if you put 10 then if a 
              subboard will only allow access levels of 11-31 to view it
              then the files will not be listed, but if the subboard had
              an access range of 10-31 then the access level is a valid
              access level so the files will be listed. An example is the
              following: on my system I have internet access with the users
              having access level of 15, they have a subboard they use which
              they can place files there. I have this subboard set to access
              level 15-31. With VegFL, since I do not want these files listed
              I set the access level in VegFL.cfg to 10. 
              
              Other subboards that will be skipped are QWK subboards, and
              invitation only areas. On my system, some users have "home"
              subboards. They want the access set for all to see, but only
              allow people in that they have invited. As these are usually
              files downloaded from Aminet only available until another user
              has downloaded the file, I don't want those files listed.
              
              
VegFL.lst  is  produced and will exist in the same directory VegFL resides.
Rename  it to whatever you want (eg.  MyBBS.txt).  It is the actual list of
files.

